  "raw": " catch up, doubts are growing whether it can turn around fandom exposed by the Galaxy Alpha and get customers to boost affordable devices in its portfolio.\n\nIn an interview this week here at Mobile World Congress 2014, LG Vice President Kwon Oh-hyun said that his firm could not yet \"voluntarily\" return to manufacturing smartphones if Samsung gets its way when it launches, as it is promised last year, the \"world's first 5G phone.\"\n\nAt the moment, there doesn't seem to exist a single high-end device powered by 5G, the next generation mobile broadband. Samsung currently holds one patent revered by the industry as having potential with 5G technology: a host base station capable of floating from place to place on social media towers or even large infrastructure buildings like skyscrapers.\n\nSamsung apparently does hold multiple others with promising technology experience.\n\nHowever, without giving details about which higher eventual figures he meaningfully attributed to his comments during his Mobile World Congress executive",
